// A shape to draw for training (REQUESTS 26): an old French print's quarter rest is a "z" with a
// knob at each end (the top knob on the right, the bottom knob on the left, the stroke between them
// bent once), not the modern zigzag. Holmes, "Aubade-Habanera" (20 Melodies No. 2), the OMR's
// development set data/dev/lieder/holmes-melodies2, scan, page 2: the left hand's lower voice ends
// nearly every bar with this rest, below the bass staff. The OMR's detector, taught only Lily#'s
// zigzag, sees no rest there at all (about 45 notes of that page set are missed). Bars 1-2 are that
// left hand (two voices); bar 3 is the same rest in one voice, in the middle of the staff. Today
// lysc draws every one of these quarter rests as the modern zigzag.
title "Z Rest"
octave absolute
time 2/2
key c major

part lh { clef bass }

section Piece {
  lh {
    voice { r2 <g, c e g>4@staccato <g, c e>4@staccato } { <c, g,>2~ <c, g,>4 r4 } |
    voice { r2 <g, c e g>4@staccato <g, c e>4@staccato } { <c, c>2~ <c, c>4 r4 } |
    c4 r4 e4 r4 |
  }
}

form { ~Piece }

score {
  staff lh "Piano"
}
